index 0000000..816f421
--- /dev/null
+++ b/vendor/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,38 @@
+# Vendored third-party JavaScript libraries
+
+These libraries are bundled locally so that ShiftPro works fully offline inside
+the Android WebView and never needs to load remote code at runtime. This is
+required for the production Android build:
+
+- The Android WebView must not fetch untrusted remote scripts that handle
+  sensitive employee data (attendance, salary, working hours).
+- The application is designed to be offline-first.
+- Removing the CDN fallback eliminates a remote-code-injection surface.
+
+## Libraries
+
+| File               | Library       | Version | Upstream                                                          | License |
+|--------------------|---------------|---------|-------------------------------------------------------------------|---------|
+| xlsx.full.min.js   | SheetJS (xlsx)| 0.18.5  | https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/xlsx@0.18.5/dist/xlsx.full.min.js    | Apache-2.0 |
+| chart.umd.min.js   | Chart.js      | 4.4.1   | https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/chart.js@4.4.1/dist/chart.umd.min.js | MIT    |
+| jspdf.umd.min.js   | jsPDF         | 2.5.1   | https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/jspdf@2.5.1/dist/jspdf.umd.min.js    | MIT    |
+| html2canvas.min.js | html2canvas   | 1.4.1   | https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/html2canvas@1.4.1/dist/html2canvas.min.js | MIT |
+
+## Verification
+
+Re-download a file and compare against the committed copy to detect tampering:
+
+```sh
+curl -fsSL https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/xlsx@0.18.5/dist/xlsx.full.min.js | diff - xlsx.full.min.js
+curl -fsSL https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/chart.js@4.4.1/dist/chart.umd.min.js | diff - chart.umd.min.js
+curl -fsSL https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/jspdf@2.5.1/dist/jspdf.umd.min.js | diff - jspdf.umd.min.js
+curl -fsSL https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/html2canvas@1.4.1/dist/html2canvas.min.js | diff - html2canvas.min.js
+```
+
+## Updating
+
+1. Bump the version in the loader comment inside `js/backup.js`, `js/charts.js`,
+   `js/pdf-export.js`, and `js/reports.js`.
+2. Replace the file in this directory with the new version.
+3. Re-run the diff commands above to confirm integrity.
+4. Run `npm test` to confirm tests still pass.
